Add missing <cstdint> for int32_t (fixes build on musl).

UnlimitedUnsigned.h uses int32_t (via PartType) but relies on it being
pulled in transitively. glibc's <vector>/<string> happen to include it;
musl does not, so the build fails with "'int32_t' does not name a type".
Include <cstdint> explicitly.
--- a/src/Base/UnlimitedUnsigned.h
+++ b/src/Base/UnlimitedUnsigned.h
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #endif
 #include <vector>
 #include <string>
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <stdexcept>
 
 // ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
